   \[
   \frac{3.2 \times 10^{-4}}{1.6 \times 10^{-4}} = 2
   \]
   This shows that the rate is directly proportional to the concentration of \( B_2 \), so \( m = 1 \).

2. **Compare the rate when [A] doubles while [B₂] remains the same (between Exp. 2 and Exp. 3):**
