   \[
   \frac{0.00401 \text{ mol}}{128.17 \text{ g/mol}} = \frac{0.6216 \text{ g/mol}}{M_{\text{Unknown}}}
   \]

5. **Solve for \( M_{\text{Unknown}} \)**:
   \[
   M_{\text{Unknown}} = \frac{0.6216 \text{ g/mol} \times 128.17 \text{ g/mol}}{0.00401 \text{ mol}}
   \]
   \[
   M_{\text{Unknown}} = \frac{79.9 \text{ g/mol}}{0.00401 \text{ mol}}
   \]
   \[
   M_{\text{Unknown}} = 19.9 \text{ g/mol}
   \]

6. **Calculate the change of atomic weight**:
   The change of atomic weight is:
   \[
   \Delta M = \frac{M_2}{n_2}
   \]
