   - The hyperplane \( H \) passing through \( 0 \) is defined by the equation \( y \cdot x = 0 \), where \( y \in (\mathbb{R}^n)^* \).  
   - The hyperplane \( H \) divides \( \mathbb{R}^n \) into two half-spaces: \( \mathbb{R}^n = H \cup H^+ \cup H^{-} \), where \( H^+ = \{x \in \mathbb{R}^n : y \cdot x > 0\} \) and \( H^- = \{x \in \mathbb{R}^n : y \cdot x < 0\} \).  
   - Since \( C \) is a cone, it is closed in \( \mathbb{R}^n \).  
   - Since \( b \notin C \), \( b \) is not in \( C \).  
