Total area of paving stones = 165 × Area of one paving stone
Total area of paving stones = 165 × (2.5 m × width)
Total area of paving stones = 412.5 m × width

Now, we set the total area of the paving stones equal to the area of the courtyard:
412.5 m × width = 825 m²

Now, we solve for the width of each paving stone:
Width = 825 m² / 412.5 m
Width = 2 m

So, the width of each paving stone is $\boxed{2}$  meters.",fluency,"# Task Description
