   - The only pair of consecutive integers that are both perfect powers are \( 1 \) and \( 2 \), but \( 1 \times 2 = 2 \) is not a perfect power.
   - The next pair of consecutive integers that are perfect powers are \( 16 \) and \( 17 \), but \( 16 \times 17 \) is not a perfect power.
