","The index of refraction (R) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a medium (v) to the speed of light in a vacuum (v₀):

R = v / v₀

In this case, the speed of light in the plate is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum, so v = 0.680 * v₀.

Therefore, the index of refraction is:

R = (0.680 * v₀) / v₀
R = 0.680

